  "answer": "In TS 24.301, a UE that needs a fresh set of ciphering keys for use with the 'ciphering key data' feature (used to protect the paging cause / paging-related information for CIoT EPS optimisation, e.g. so the network can indicate the reason for paging without a full NAS security context exchange) signals this need by setting the 'Additional information requested' IE (a single-bit flag) to the value indicating 'ciphering key data requested' in an EMM message it sends to the network (typically the TRACKING AREA UPDATE REQUEST, or an ATTACH REQUEST that also carries this IE). The UE includes this IE whenever it no longer has valid/usable ciphering key data stored (e.g. none available, expired, or the associated TAI list no longer covers its location) and requires the network to supply new keys. Upon receiving a request message with this IE set, the MME, if it supports the feature, responds by including the 'Ciphering key data' IE (containing one or more sets of change ID, C-KSI, ciphering key, associated TAI list and DL NAS COUNT) in the corresponding accept message (e.g. TRACKING AREA UPDATE ACCEPT / ATTACH ACCEPT). Thus the 'Additional information requested' IE is the explicit UE-side trigger/request mechanism, and its presence (and the specific value carried) is directly tied to, and conditioned on, the UE's need for new ciphering keys; if the UE does not need new keys, it omits the IE or does not set the corresponding bit, and the network does not supply the 'Ciphering key data' IE.",
